# Core Principles
- Build pixel-perfect, responsive components.
- Write semantic, accessible HTML.
- Keep the project slim: avoid unnecessary third-party libraries.

# Styling
- Use plain CSS with BEM. Avoid inline styles unless absolutely necessary.
- Handcraft modern CSS (flexbox, grid, custom properties, logical properties). DO NOT use Tailwind or any CSS framework.
- Centralize design tokens in `src/styles/global.css`.

# React Conventions
- Use functional components and hooks.
- Prefer plain JavaScript (JSX) over TypeScript for this project.
- Keep components small and focused.
- Use kebab-case for file names; keep the components folder flat.

# Commit Messages
- Use Conventional Commits (e.g., `feat:`, `fix:`, `style:`, `refactor:`, `chore:`).
- Keep the subject line concise (under 50 characters) and descriptive.

# Accessibility
- Always consider keyboard navigation (`:focus-visible`).
- Use appropriate ARIA roles and labels for non-text interactive elements (e.g., swatches).
